   \[
   1024 \div 7 = 146 \text{ remainder } 2
   \]
   This means:
   \[
   1024 = 7 \times 146 + 2
   \]
   Therefore, the remainder when \(1024\) is divided by \(7\) is \(2\).

So, the remainder when \(2^{10}\) is divided by \(7\) is \(\boxed{2}\).
